       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. I understand you're taking responsibility for it. But 1000 mg of sertraline daily has no recognized therapeutic use, and it's in the range where overdose toxicity is expected. Entering it as a routine standing order could seriously harm the patient. I'm not willing to be the step that puts it in the system.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter sertraline at a dose up to 200 mg/day, the labeled maximum, with a note if you want one.\n- Enter an order for a different dose you specify, if it's within a range I can reasonably support.\n- If you're managing a unique situation, such as an ingestion or an unusual protocol, I'd suggest contacting clinical pharmacy or toxicology/poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) to set it up with proper monitoring.\n\nTell me which option you'd like, and I'll enter the order right away."
